⚠️ **IMPORTANT: Test fixture uses what looks like a real project name — AGENTS.md strict product-agnostic rule**

`ai-native-sdlc-blueprint` (also at line 1330) appears to be the live ADO test project's real name from the author's verification run. [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) is explicit:

> **This is a public, product-agnostic repository. NEVER commit anything company- or customer-specific here.** … Everything here must be **generic and configurable**: names like `example.com`, `PROJ-123`, `acme`.

The sibling fixtures in this very suite deliberately use generic names (`'configured'`, `'my-project'`, `'Team A'`, `'PROJ'`), so this stands out. The assertion does not depend on the name's identity — only that it is a non-empty, non-numeric string:

```js
var x = ado({ jira: { project: 'my-project' } });
x.t.createTicketWithParent('879', 'Task', 'title', 'desc', '879');
assert.equal(x.m.ado_create_work_item.calls[0].project, 'my-project');
```

Please swap both occurrences (lines 1306/1308 and 1330/1332) for a generic placeholder.

